    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters May 15th with a primary objective of exploiting favorable matchups for our high-upside speed threats. The strongest play on the board is **Corbin Carroll** (79.89), who benefits from a prime matchup against Freeland\u2019s 4.25 xERA and a significant park factor boost. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) are elite starts today; **Mickey Moniak** in particular is primed for a multi-steal opportunity given the favorable park factor and a opposing starter in Kelly who has proven susceptible to base runners. **Josh Naylor** (73.91) also offers immense value as our anchor in the cleanup role, benefiting from a soft matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez, making him our most reliable bet for RBI production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Seiya Suzuki** (58.81), who narrowly missed the starting cut despite a solid projection. While his profile is strong, the optimization model favored **Henry Bolte** (59.11) due to the higher projected offensive environment in the Mahle start, leaving **Seiya Suzuki** on the pine as a high-floor insurance policy. Conversely, **Austin Riley** (44.64) was an easy sit given his struggle against Early\u2019s profile, and **Travis Bazzana** remains on the bench due to a negative platoon split against Abbott. We continue to monitor the status of **Jose Caballero**, who remains sidelined on the IL, as we look to maximize our daily efficiency and maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings. \n\nManagers should remain alert regarding the lower-scoring plays at the bottom of the lineup. **Zach McKinstry** (43.80) and **Cole Young** (48.66) are effectively operating at our basement floor, and both represent candidates for replacement if our game-cap strategy requires further preservation. While we are starting **Gabriel Moreno** (60.44) and **Dalton Rushing** (56.81), their scores are tethered to the defensive utility and holding potential against opposing baserunners; keep a close eye on any late-inning weather alerts, though no major storms are currently flagged for our primary venue sites.",
